{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_dkydrly2hgfanl6ymsz76g2gcyd3dw5pascjzvarkeqmdybmrl5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## What I found and fixed\n\nThe translation was structurally complete (all 22 symbols present, no stubs), but had **6 floating-point operand-order bugs**. The C is compiled at `-O0`, so nothing is inlined — every `c2Dot`/`c2Add`/`c2Mulvs`/`c2MulmvT` call is a real `call`, and `addss`/`mulss` return the **destination** operand when both operands are NaN. I read the C disassembly to recover the exact destination register of every float op:\n\n| function | C codegen | pre-fix Rust |\n|---|---|---|\n| `c2Dot` | `mulss` dest = `a.x` / **`b.y`**; `addss` dest = the **y** product | dest = `a.y`; `addss` dest = x product |\n| `c2Add` | `addss` dest = `b`, both lanes | dest = `a` internally (wrapper disagreed with helper) |\n| `c2Mulvs` | `mulss` dest = `a`, **both** lanes | dest = `b` in the y lane |\n| `c2MulmvT` | dest = matrix entry / `b.y`; `addss` dest = 2nd product | three wrong orders, wrapper ≠ helper |\n| `c2RaytoAABB` ×4 | `out->t`: `mulss` dest = **`A.t`** | dest = `tN` |\n| `c2RaytoCapsule` | `y`: `addss` dest = the product; `out->t`: dest = `A.t` | dest = `yAp.y`; dest = `t` |\n\nI also removed the duplicated arithmetic in the `c2Add`/`c2MulmvT` export wrappers — that duplication was how two of the divergences got in.\n\n## Artifacts (in `translation/`)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 22 C symbols, 22 Rust, **0 missing, 0 extra**, 0 undefined non-libc.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 42 rows, all with passing tests. Testing corrected 5 of my own predictions (e.g. `gen_ray` with `mp == ray.p` returns **4**, not 0 — the AABB cast still hits because `da0..da3` read the finite `p0`, not the NaN `p1`).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 70 rows, all `[x]`, ~600k randomized cases.\n- **`tests/`** — 55 tests, both `.so`s loaded via `libloading`, all floats compared with `to_bits()`.\n\n## Notable\n\n- **Branch coverage is proven**, not assumed: classifiers recompute each predicate *using the C library's own exports*. All 10 capsule branches, all 6 AABB branches, all 4 circle branches, and all 8 `gen_ray` hit-bit values are reached.\n- **Non-vacuity proven**: reverting one operand order makes 5 tests fail; restoring it returns 27/27.\n- **One row can't be asserted bit-exactly** — `c2CastRay` with an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` falls off the end of a non-`void` function (no `default:`, no trailing `return`). The compiled C does `ja → leave; ret`, returning the *caller's leftover `%eax`*. No Rust value can match that, so the test asserts what *is* well-defined (neither crashes, neither writes through `out`, compared against a sentinel) and documents the rest. I deliberately did **not** invent a matching constant.\n- `c2RaytoAABB`'s `hit == 0` branch is **unreachable with finite inputs** (`da/(da-db) ≤ 1` always); it needs NaN in *both* lanes of `A.p`. That assertion lives in the bit-pattern fuzz row, which hits it 570/20000 times.\n- No binary target exists (`add_library(... SHARED)` only), so there is no stdout to compare.\n\nFinal state: **6/6 configurations green** (`--no-default-features`, `--all-features`, default × debug/release), 55 tests each. Re-run with `cd translation && ./run_diff_tests.sh`.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: fidelity here rests on the `asm!`-based `fadd`/`fmul` helpers pinning operand order, which is x86-64-specific — on other architectures the code falls back to plain `a + b` and NaN-payload equivalence would no longer be guaranteed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6163,"cache_read_input_tokens":217101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6163,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a252d8f-9b33-4ad6-b5b8-1dd90a964666","uuid":"48d1fbe7-c50b-497c-b304-0db717ec8e88","timestamp":"2026-09-05T07:48:00.761Z"}
